---
import { linesFor, paymentsFor, lineValue, money, raw101 } from './model.mjs';
const lines = linesFor(101);
const payments = paymentsFor(101);
---
<figure class="qr-figure" aria-labelledby="multiplication-title">
 <figcaption id="multiplication-title"><span>Figure 3</span>Two lines × two payments = four result rows</figcaption>
 <div class="qr-panel">
  <table class="qr-matrix"><caption class="qr-tag">Order 101 · each cell is one joined row</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Order line ↓<br/>Payment →</th>{payments.map(p => <th scope="col">{p.id}<br/>{money(p.amount)}</th>)}</tr></thead><tbody>{lines.map(i => <tr><th scope="row">Line {i.line} · {i.product}<br/>{money(lineValue(i))}</th>{payments.map(p => <td><strong>101 · {i.line} · {p.id}</strong><span>Line {money(lineValue(i))}</span><span>Paid {money(p.amount)}</span></td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table>
  <div class="qr-totals"><div><span>SUM of line values</span><strong>{money(raw101.reduce((s,r) => s+r.value,0))}</strong><span>Each line appears twice</span></div><div><span>SUM of payments</span><strong>{money(raw101.reduce((s,r) => s+r.paid,0))}</strong><span>Each payment appears twice</span></div></div>
 </div>
 <p class="qr-note">The real line total is 39.50 and the real paid total is 39.50. The joined rows total 79.00 on each side. Every pair of line and payment is different; DISTINCT over these five selected columns removes nothing.</p>
</figure>
